AB  - A 53-year-old woman presented with complaints of blurred vision in the left eye. She had been treated for recurrent non-functioning pituitary adenoma (NEPA). A vitreous biopsy followed by histopathologic examination showed the presence of Candida albicans. Meanwhile, Cushing's disease was diagnosed and gamma knife surgery was performed. Vitrectomy and antifungal treatment improved ocular infection and inflammation. Herein, we describe the first case of C albicans endophthalmitis in a patient with NEPA evolving into Cushing's disease. (C) 2014 The Authors. International Society for Human and Animal Mycology. Published by Elsevier B.V.
